Session: 2026-10-15 14:17 UTC
Plan: plan/2026/09/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate.md
Scope: P18-V01 Remoting connectTimeoutMillis Bootstrap timing slice

Source review
- Compared pinned Java NettyRemotingClient.start(), fetchBootstrap(), and
  createBootstrap() with Rust RemotingClient startup and connection selection.
- Java configures direct Bootstrap at start; proxy Bootstrap is created and
  cached on first use per CIDR, reading the then-current config value.
- Rust previously used only the start snapshot for direct and proxy dials, and
  NameServer scans imposed an extra deadline that did not match Bootstrap
  timeout behavior when the configured value was zero or changed for a proxy.

Implementation
- Code commit: aca955cd fix(remoting): match proxy bootstrap timeout timing.
- Rust now snapshots direct timeout at start, caches live timeout on first
  matched proxy-CIDR use, reuses that value for that CIDR, and reads newer
  values for later CIDRs. Reachability scans use an optional operation deadline
  so zero means no separate connect cap.
- Added Rust tests for post-start proxy timeout capture/cache, proxy scan
  timeout sampling, and zero-timeout NameServer scanning.
- Extended Java RemotingLiveConfigProbe to verify direct start-time capture,
  cached proxy reuse, and first-use capture for another CIDR.
- Updated the connectTimeoutMillis row in
  docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md and appended this revision's
  evidence to docs/release-checklist.md. No plan files were edited.

Verification
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features --locked`: passed;
  88 unit, 6 codec, 1 fuzz regression, 5 security, 93 transport, 5 doctests.
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-targets --all-features
  --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: passed.
- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: passed; 37 scenarios,
  Remoting live-config probe, Java/Rust cross-decodes and fixture checks.
- `git diff --check`: passed before code commit.

Status
- The connectTimeoutMillis Bootstrap timing row is closed on aca955cd.
- Broad P18-V01, full-workspace P18-V02 gates on the eventual final revision,
  current-revision GitHub Ubuntu/P18-V04 evidence, Phase 19 local Docker/Broker
  automation, and release version/registry checks remain open. Owner-run
  deployment/live Broker checks remain manual Phase 19 validation.
- Branch phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate is local and ahead of
  origin; no push, tag, publication, or live Broker action was performed.

Session: 2026-10-15 14:39 UTC
Plan: plan/2026/09/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate.md
Scope: P18-V01 Remoting per-channel idle-timeout and worker-group setting timing

Source review
- Compared pinned Java channel pipeline initialization with Rust's connection
  creation and processor-worker startup paths.
- Java reads `clientChannelMaxIdleTimeSeconds` and
  `disableNettyWorkerGroup` while each channel pipeline is initialized. Rust
  previously captured both at construction and could not reflect later Java
  config changes.

Implementation
- Code commit: b37d8522 fix(remoting): read channel settings per connection.
- Added live Rust adapters. Each new connection samples both values before
  dialing; existing connections keep their initialized idle timer and dispatch
  path. The worker pool starts at client start so later channels can choose
  either dispatch mode.
- Rust loopback tests cover post-start setting changes and existing-channel
  retention. Java `RemotingLiveConfigProbe` checks the new channel's idle
  handler and executor selection.
- Updated the two setting rows in
  `docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md` and appended evidence to
  `docs/release-checklist.md`. No plan files were edited.

Verification
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-features --locked`: passed;
  89 unit, 6 codec, 1 fuzz regression, 5 security, 95 transport, 5 doctests.
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --all-targets --all-features
  --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: passed.
- `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: passed; 37 scenarios,
  Remoting live-config probe, Java/Rust cross-decodes and fixture checks.
- `git diff --check`: passed before code commit; documentation diff check is
  recorded with the following documentation commit.

Status
- The two Remoting setting-timing rows are closed on b37d8522.
- Broad P18-V01, final-revision full-workspace P18-V02 gates, current-revision
